@id n1_choira
# DRAFT
# Brother Wulfric, the oldest of the choir, on the south walk at dusk (night 1). Background; short and crabbed.
== start
(An old brother of the choir on the south walk, rubbing his knees against the cold.)
Wulfric {weary}: So you're the porter. Ring Matins on the mark, boy. Old knees need warning.
-> topics

== again
Wulfric {weary}: The bell, boy. On the mark.
-> topics

== topics
* [if not n1_choira_long] How long have you sung here, brother? -> long

== long [set n1_choira_long]
Wulfric {amused}: Forty years. I've seen porters come, and I've seen them go. Most of them go.
-> end

== leave
Wulfric {weary}: On the mark, mind.
